Am I the only person who finds this really, really, really, REALLY
obnoxious, that the bad guys can teleport away, even when on levels 
where teleportation is verboten?  I chased Asmodeus up to dungeon 
level *20* one time with a samurai, because as I would close with
the stairs he would run up them.  Later, a hasted demon (Jubilex?
It was in Gehennom) would teleport in, hit me, and teleport away
before I could take a single move.  Step, *poof* bap bap *poof*,
step, *poof* etc.  The wizard would do this too, except when he 
tried to steal something from me he would try to teleport and fail,
leaving me one whack before he _succeeded_ due to getting hurt.

NH3.1 introduced more parity between what monsters can do and what
adventurers can do, with wands, potions, etc.  What's good for the
goose is good for the gander; either there's teleportation on a
level or there isn't.

